      "sample_index": 7,
      "text": "To find the exponent of 3 in the prime factorization of 24!, we need to count how many times 3 appears as a factor in the numbers from 1 to 24. We can do this by dividing 24 by 3 and then dividing the result by 3 again, and so on, until we get a number less than 3. Then, we multiply these quotients together to get the exponent of 3 in the prime factorization of 24!.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Exponent of 3} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{3} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{3^2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{24}{3^3} \\right\\rfloor + \\cdots\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\n# Calculate the exponent of 3 in the prime factorization of 24!\ndef exponent_of_prime_in_factorial(n, p):\n    exponent = 0\n    power = p\n    while power <= n:\n        exponent += n // power\n        power *= p\n    return exponent\n\n# Calculate the exponent of 3 in 24!\nexponent_of_3 = exponent_of_prime_in_factorial(24, 3)\nprint(exponent_of_3)\n```\n```output\n10\n```\nThe exponent of 3 in the prime factorization of \\(24!\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
